  "text_pages": [
    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - a. Seoul Campus Dorms\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nHUFS Housing\nHUFS Dormitories\nSeoul Campus\nHUFS offers its students various housing options. Though International Houses are technically \"off\" campus, they are directly across the street from the front or rear gate of campus. There is little to no difference in the commute time to various buildings/classrooms around campus. These are:\nOn-Campus Housing\nGlobeeDorm\nManaged by HUFS (All exchange students must contact OIAM for any Globee Dorm related inquiries and NOT the Globee Dorm office)\nOff-Campus Housing\nInternational House A\nInternational House\nC\nInternational House\nE\nInternational Houses are all directly m\nanaged by the OIAM (\nContact point: visiting@hufs.ac.kr\n)\nGlobeeDorm\nis a typical dormitory while\nInternational House A / C /\nE\nare apartment units. Fees for each housing option vary but a general overview is provided below on each dorm page.\nDormitory Assignments\nYou will be notified about dormitory assignments about one month before the semester begins by email. We will not be able to tell you about room availability until current students move out at the end of the summer/winter session, and know how many students are returning for the regular semester.\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  ],
